  "body": "Decentralized Identifiers (DID) is a specification on the standards track, being developed in a W3C Working Group - more details here: https://w3c.github.io/did-core/. This change would allow apps and extensions to register as a `did:` URL handler and handle various DID wallet/management-related tasks for users.\r\n\r\n> Note: one of the major browser vendor companies, Microsoft, will be rolling out support for this family of technologies very soon.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#custom-handlers:safelisted-scheme\r\n\r\n```diff\r\nbitcoin\r\n+did\r\ngeo\r\nim\r\nirc\r\nircs\r\nmagnet\r\nmailto\r\nmms\r\nnews\r\nnntp\r\nopenpgp4fpr\r\nsip\r\nsms\r\nsmsto\r\nssh\r\ntel\r\nurn\r\nwebcal\r\nwtai\r\nxmpp\r\n```",
